  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-19T15:33:10.715Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The actual controls used for hand tracking are legitimately dangerous for anyone with underlying hand/wrist injuries. \n\nPinch ones finger+thumb and flicking them forward is an actual exercise used to irritate and provoke a reaction from anyone with tendonitis/carpal tunnel in their wrist and can also lead to the development of said condition.\n\nBasically hand tracking is designed in a way that it will cause long term damage to the users hands.\n\nAs someone who is undergoing hand therapy and seeing an orthopedist for the past 2 years and needs to do similar motions to confirm yes, I am still experiencing these problems.\n\nAnd as someone who has explained these control methods to said orthopedist/therapist who responded with \"that is the most awful thing anyone could be doing to their hand/wrist please don't do that anymore\". \n\nPlease consult an orthopedist regarding this control method.",
